Alembic migrations for the ingestion service's PostgreSQL schema.

ADR 0010 chose Alembic running hand-written SQL and no declared models, so
`alembic revision --autogenerate` does not work here and never will: it needs
model metadata to diff against. Write `op.execute("...")` by hand.

    alembic revision -m "What it does" --rev-id 0002
    alembic upgrade head
    alembic downgrade -1

The database is named by DATABASE_URL, or by `sqlalchemy.url` set on the config
object by a caller that already knows it. `alembic.ini` deliberately leaves it
empty. See `env.py`.

ADR 0012 records the schema and why each table looks the way it does.
